  <h2>Question 1 — Scale Your Application (5 Marks)</h2>

  <h3>1(a) Peak-Demand Situation & Docker Compose Cluster Deployment (1 Mark)</h3>
  <p><strong>Peak-Demand Scenario:</strong> In a residential university with over 5,000 students across multiple hostel blocks, the critical peak-demand window occurs during the <strong>Dinner Rush (8:30 PM to 9:15 PM)</strong>. Thousands of students finish their meal and simultaneously open MessHub to check tomorrow's breakfast menu and rate dinner quality.</p>
  <p><strong>Hardest-Hit API:</strong> <code>GET /api/menu</code> (Read-heavy surge) and <code>POST /api/feedback</code> (Write surge). <code>GET /api/menu</code> absorbs over 100+ requests per second.</p>
  <p><strong>Docker Compose Cluster:</strong> Three backend instances deployed behind an <strong>Nginx reverse proxy / load balancer</strong> on Port <code>80</code>, connected to MongoDB Atlas.</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Container Name</th>
      <th>Service</th>
      <th>Image</th>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Port Mappings</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>mess_nginx_lb</code></td>
      <td>nginx</td>
      <td><code>nginx:alpine</code></td>
      <td>Up</td>
      <td>0.0.0.0:80-&gt;80/tcp</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>mess_backend_1</code></td>
      <td>backend1</td>
      <td><code>mess-backend:hardened</code></td>
      <td>Up (Healthy)</td>
      <td>0.0.0.0:5001-&gt;5000/tcp</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>mess_backend_2</code></td>
      <td>backend2</td>
      <td><code>mess-backend:hardened</code></td>
      <td>Up (Healthy)</td>
      <td>0.0.0.0:5002-&gt;5000/tcp</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>mess_backend_3</code></td>
      <td>backend3</td>
      <td><code>mess-backend:hardened</code></td>
      <td>Up (Healthy)</td>
      <td>0.0.0.0:5003-&gt;5000/tcp</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

