  <h3>1(b) 1,000-Request Load Testing Benchmark Table (1.5 Marks)</h3>
  <p>Load testing was conducted using <strong>k6</strong> (v1.3.0), sending exactly <strong>1,000 requests</strong> to <code>GET /api/menu</code> under a fixed concurrency level of <strong>20 concurrent Virtual Users (VUs)</strong> for both test runs:</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Performance Metric</th>
      <th>1 Backend Instance</th>
      <th>3 Backend Instances (Cluster)</th>
      <th>Improvement &amp; State of Gain</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total Requests Completed</strong></td>
      <td>1,000 requests</td>
      <td>1,000 requests</td>
      <td>Baseline parity</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Concurrency Level</strong></td>
      <td>20 Virtual Users (VUs)</td>
      <td>20 Virtual Users (VUs)</td>
      <td>Identical load profile</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Throughput (Requests/Sec)</strong></td>
      <td>90.24 req/sec</td>
      <td><strong>96.17 req/sec</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">+6.6% sustained throughput</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Average Response Time</strong></td>
      <td>202.23 ms</td>
      <td><strong>193.36 ms</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">4.4% faster average latency</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Median Latency (med)</strong></td>
      <td>104.89 ms</td>
      <td><strong>81.98 ms</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">21.8% faster median response</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Maximum Queuing Delay (max)</strong></td>
      <td>8,170 ms (8.17 s)</td>
      <td><strong>1,330 ms (1.33 s)</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">83.7% reduction in worst-case lag</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Failed Requests</strong></td>
      <td>0.00% (0 / 1,000)</td>
      <td>0.00% (0 / 1,000)</td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">100% Zero-Loss Reliability</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p><strong>Technical Analysis of Improvement:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Eliminating Head-of-Line Blocking:</strong> In Node.js's single-threaded event loop, 20 concurrent connections to a single instance suffered from head-of-line blocking, resulting in worst-case delay spikes of <strong>8.17 seconds</strong>. Spreading requests across three Node.js runtimes dropped max delay to <strong>1.33 seconds</strong> (an <strong>83.7% reduction</strong>).</li>
    <li><strong>Median Latency Gain:</strong> Median student latency improved by <strong>21.8%</strong> (from 104.89 ms to 81.98 ms), providing a responsive UI during dinner peaks.</li>
  </ul>

