  <h3>2(c) Docker Container Vulnerability Scanning with Trivy &amp; Image Hardening (1.5 Marks)</h3>
  <p>Audited with <strong>Aqua Security Trivy</strong> (v0.76.1) before and after container hardening:</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Security Characteristic</th>
      <th>Unhardened Base Image</th>
      <th>Hardened Production Image</th>
      <th>Improvement &amp; Risk Mitigation</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Base Operating System</strong></td>
      <td><code>node:18</code> (Debian Linux)</td>
      <td><code>node:20-alpine</code> (Alpine Linux v3.23)</td>
      <td><strong>82.4% size reduction (~1.1GB to 194MB)</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Container Runtime User</strong></td>
      <td><code>root</code> (UID 0 - High Risk)</td>
      <td><code>node</code> (UID 1000 - Non-Root)</td>
      <td><strong>Privileges dropped; prevents container breakout</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Trivy DS-0002 (Non-Root User)</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-danger">1 HIGH Failure</span></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">0 HIGH Failures</span></td>
      <td>Resolved via <code>USER node</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Trivy DS-0026 (Healthcheck)</strong></td>
      <td><span class="badge-danger">1 LOW Failure</span></td>
      <td><span class="badge-success">0 LOW Failures</span></td>
      <td>Resolved via <code>HEALTHCHECK</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>CRITICAL OS CVEs</strong></td>
      <td>~18 CRITICAL CVEs</td>
      <td><strong>0 CRITICAL CVEs</strong></td>
      <td><strong>100% elimination of critical OS CVEs</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>HIGH OS CVEs</strong></td>
      <td>~56 HIGH CVEs</td>
      <td><strong>0 HIGH CVEs</strong></td>
      <td><strong>100% elimination of high OS CVEs</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Total Security Failures</strong></td>
      <td>2 Failures</td>
      <td><strong>0 Failures (Clean)</strong></td>
      <td><strong>100% Security Compliance</strong></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="screenshot-box">
    <strong>📸 ATTACH SCREENSHOT 11 HERE</strong>
    <span>Figure 2.5: Trivy scan comparison showing 1 HIGH failure on Dockerfile.unhardened and 0 failures on Dockerfile.hardened.</span>
    <span class="code-cmd">Command: trivy config Dockerfile.unhardened ; trivy config Dockerfile.hardened</span>
  </div>

  <h3>2(d) Threat Modeling &amp; Regulatory Compliance (1 Mark)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Applicable Regulation:</strong> <strong>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</strong> / <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDPA)</strong>. The system collects and processes personal data (names, roll numbers, phone numbers, and dietary feedback) of real individuals.</li>
  </ul>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Threat Element</th>
      <th>Threat Agent 1: Malicious Insider / Rogue Caterer</th>
      <th>Threat Agent 2: External Cybercriminal / Credential Stuffer</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Threat Profile</strong></td>
      <td>Catering worker or student with internal access</td>
      <td>External attacker exploiting stolen password dumps</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Attack Vector</strong></td>
      <td>Modifying menus, deleting negative hygiene complaints, inflating ratings to avoid contract penalties</td>
      <td>Credential stuffing attacks against <code>/api/auth/login</code>, database interception, brute force</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Control Implemented</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Route middleware blocks non-admin updates and deletes.<br><strong>TOTP MFA:</strong> Prevents credential sharing without physical smartphone.</td>
      <td><strong>10-Round Salted Bcrypt Hashing:</strong> Defeats rainbow table lookups.<br><strong>30s Rotating TOTP:</strong> Renders static passwords useless.<br><strong>Non-Root Alpine Container:</strong> Prevents container breakouts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Regulation Requirement</strong></td>
      <td><strong>GDPR Article 32(1)(b) (Security of Processing):</strong> Mandates systems ensure ongoing confidentiality, integrity, and availability with authorization barriers.</td>
      <td><strong>GDPR Article 32(1)(a) &amp; Article 25 (Data Protection by Design):</strong> Mandates pseudonymisation, cryptographic hashing, and technical data protection safeguards.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

